{:edb/db-before-t 1255 :edb/db-after-t 1256 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534568 50 #inst "2026-10-08T01:13:56.801Z" 13194139534568 true] [17592186157023 1100 "Let $U = \\{ a, b, c, d, e, f, g \\}$ be the universal set and let $B = \\{ b, d, f \\}.$ What is $\\overline{B}?$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/assets/25f40492b0466495519d6ff94859d0cef4c206e291d31eba2a980732b497af31.png)" 13194139534568 true] [17592186157023 1100 "Let $U = \\{a, b, c, d, e, f, g \\}$ be the universal set and let $B = \\{b, d, f \\}$. What is $\\overline{B}$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2829/Source/Images/e3286d4e435a020e578a009552a1be73.png)" 13194139534568 false] [17592186157023 1145 "The complement of $B$, denoted $\\overline B$, consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $B$. To represent $\\overline B$, we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $B$, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2829/Source/Images/9385e4e8c3b0eab7bcb5e0f0d1bb2955.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $a$, $c$, $e$, and $g$. These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $B$. Therefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{B} = \\{a,c,e,g \\}\n$$" 13194139534568 false] [17592186157023 1145 "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overline B,$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $B.$ To represent $\\overline B,$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $B,$ as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14035973/assets/daad235ef63e127e99bf3eec7b7bbe75fe6adb969f5b54ebb5a3fb010773b680.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $a,$ $c,$ $e,$ and $g.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $B.$ Therefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{B} = \\{ a,c,e,g \\}.\n$$" 13194139534568 true] [17592186157024 1100 "Let $U = \\{ a, b, c, d, e, f, g \\}$ be the universal set and let $A = \\{ b, c, d, f, g \\}.$ What is $\\overline{A}?$" 13194139534568 true] [17592186157024 1100 "Let $U = \\{a, b, c, d, e, f, g \\}$ be the universal set and let $A = \\{b, c, d, f, g \\}$. What is $\\overline{A}$?" 13194139534568 false] [17592186157024 1145 "The complement of $A$, denoted $\\overline{A}$, consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A$.\n\nThe only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are $a$ and $e$.\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{A} = \\{a, e \\}\n$$" 13194139534568 false] [17592186157024 1145 "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overline{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are $a$ and $e.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{A} = \\{ a, e \\}.\n$$" 13194139534568 true] [17592186157025 1100 "Let $U = \\{ 1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 30 \\}$ be the universal set and let $B = \\{ 5, 6, 7, \\ldots, 28 \\}.$ What is $\\overline{B}?$" 13194139534568 true] [17592186157025 1100 "Let $U = \\{1, 2, 3, \\ldots, 30 \\}$ be the universal set and let $B = \\{5, 6, 7, \\ldots, 28 \\}$. What is $\\overline{B}$?" 13194139534568 false] [17592186157025 1145 "The complement of $B$, denoted $\\overline{B}$, consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B$.\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the integers $1$ through $30$, while the set $B$ consists of the integers $5$ through $28$.\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $1$, $2$, $3$, $4$, $29$, and $30$.\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{B} = \\{1,2,3,4,29,30 \\}\n$$" 13194139534568 false] [17592186157025 1145 "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overline{B},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the integers $1$ through $30,$ while the set $B$ consists of the integers $5$ through $28.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $1,$ $2,$ $3,$ $4,$ $29,$ and $30.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overline{B} = \\{ 1,2,3,4,29,30 \\}.\n$$" 13194139534568 true] [17592186157220 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295922 13194139534568 true] [17592186157220 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295929 13194139534568 true] [17592186157220 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295971 13194139534568 true] [17592186157220 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296006 13194139534568 true] [17592186157220 1020 #edb/ref 17592186296013 13194139534568 true] [17592186157221 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295936 13194139534568 true] [17592186157221 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295943 13194139534568 true] [17592186157221 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295992 13194139534568 true] [17592186157221 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295999 13194139534568 true] [17592186157222 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295950 13194139534568 true] [17592186157222 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295957 13194139534568 true] [17592186157222 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295964 13194139534568 true] [17592186157222 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295978 13194139534568 true] [17592186157222 1020 #edb/ref 17592186295985 13194139534568 true] [17592186157502 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534568 true] [17592186157502 1100 "If $U = {t, u, v, w, x, y}$ is the universal set and $S = {w, x, y}$, then the complement of $S$ is" 13194139534568 false] [17592186157502 1100 "If $U={t,u,v,w,x,y}$ is the universal set and $S={w,x,y},$ then the complement of $S$ is" 13194139534568 true] [17592186157502 1145 "The complement of $S,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{S},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $S.$\n\nThe only elements of $U$ that are not in $S$ are $t,$ $u,$ and $v.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $S$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{S}={t,u,v}.\n$$" 13194139534568 true] [17592186295922 1017 #edb/ref 17592186295923 13194139534568 true] [17592186295922 1089 "q-102243" 13194139534568 true] [17592186295922 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534568 true] [17592186295922 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_A